<title>USA: FTC seeks more details on CVS,Revco.</title>
<headline>FTC seeks more details on CVS,Revco.</headline>
<dateline>WOONSOCKET, R.I. 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>CVS Corp said Friday that it and Revco D.S. Inc received a request for additional information from the Federal Trade Commission relating to CVS' proposed acquisition of Revco.</p>
<p>The parties intend to respond promptly and do not expect the request to delay completion of the transaction by mid-year 1997. On February 7, 1997, CVS definitively agreed to buy Revco for $2.8 billion in stock and the assumption of $900 million.  </p>
<p>In April 1996, Revco and Rite Aid Corp terminated their merger agreement after antitrust regulators opposed the deal on the grounds that it could drive up drug prices.</p>
</text>
